  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/a9ce171a-9e43-413c-a1c7-3a1777f92b29-9894244.PNG\" style=\"width: 180px; height: 128px;\" /></p><p>The equation of line&nbsp;passing through the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and parallel to a line with direction ratios <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;will be,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>&#955;</mi></math></p><p>Now let any point on the line will be,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>&#955;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>We know the direction ratios of the line joining the points&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is given by</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Therefore, the direction ratios of line PM,</p><p>D.R of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>PM</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>&#955;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Since, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>PM</mi></math> is perpendicular to the line</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>&#955;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Now distance of point P from point M,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>PM</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>PM</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>14</mn></msqrt></math></p>",
